sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User / Terminal
    participant CLI as cli.py
    participant Config as config.py
    participant Parser as parser.py
    participant Models as models.py
    participant Analyzer as analyzer.py
    participant Ollama as Ollama Server (Local API)

    User->>CLI: python cli.py resources/application.log --last 20
    Note over CLI: Execution begins in main()

    CLI->>Config: Read defaults (DEFAULT_MODEL = "llama3.2", OLLAMA_URL = "http://localhost:11434")
    CLI->>Parser: parse_file("resources/application.log")

    loop For each non-empty line in log file
        Parser->>Parser: _parse_line(raw_line)
        Parser->>Parser: Extract regex groups & key=value metadata
        Parser->>Models: Instantiate LogEntry(timestamp, level, service, message, metadata)
        Models-->>Parser: LogEntry instance
    end

    Parser-->>CLI: list[LogEntry] (65 entries)
    Note over CLI: Slice list to last 20 entries (entries[-20:])

    CLI->>Analyzer: analyze(entries, model="llama3.2", ollama_url="http://localhost:11434")
    Analyzer->>Analyzer: _build_prompt(entries) once

    loop Up to 3 attempts for invalid LLM output
        Analyzer->>Ollama: POST /api/generate {"model": "llama3.2", "prompt": "...", "stream": false, "format": "json"}
        Ollama-->>Analyzer: JSON response envelope
        Analyzer->>Analyzer: json.loads(data["response"])
        Analyzer->>Models: IncidentAnalysis.model_validate(parsed JSON)
        Models-->>Analyzer: Validated IncidentAnalysis
    end

    Analyzer-->>CLI: IncidentAnalysis
    CLI-->>User: Print validated incident report

    Note over Analyzer,CLI: LLMParseError and LLMValidationError retry. Connection, timeout, and HTTP errors reach the CLI, which prints an error and exits with status 1.
